       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** the labeled maximum for adults is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. That is usually 850 mg three times daily. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day. The ordered amount is about twice that.\n- **Risk:** a dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease confirm what you intended. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what was meant.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, if you meant something else.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
